Findings:
- F-SG124-1: packet premise "enrich/ has no cost symbol" is FALSE as written (synthesize.py carries INPUT_USD_PER_1M /
  OUTPUT_USD_PER_1M / estimate_text_cost / SYNTHESIS_PER_CALL_CAP_USD). The narrower premise about jina.py is TRUE. Resolved by
  extension: the Jina rate is a distinct vendor/unit added beside the Jina client, never a duplicate of estimate_text_cost.
- F-SG124-2: the vendor pricing page moved (/pricing -> /api-dashboard/pricing/) and is an SPA whose pack prices come from
  dash.jina.ai/api/v1/product. Extra keyless egress beyond the packet's "single GET" is a deviation, justified by the packet's
  own "page moved" clause; no auth, no metered call.
- F-SG124-3: no single official token->USD price is stated; pack prices span $0.0169-$1.00/1M. The constant uses the base
  currently-offered pack ($0.05/1M, the higher of the two offered) as a conservative upper bound.
- F-SG124-4: "starting from 10,000 tokens" is a minimum, not a ceiling. The estimator default is the vendor minimum and accepts a
  larger caller-supplied token bound; it does not claim to be a proven ceiling on tokens.
- F-SG124-5 (minor, CO-08/CO-83): AGENTS.md binds no {{VENV}}, {{VTEST}}, {{EVIDENCE_DIR}} (they ride lang/python.md). I used the
  real interpreter path backend/venv/bin/python and the packet-named commands; no value was invented.
- F-SG124-6 (carried, outside scope): STATE.md:2 still reads contract 0.36.0 while AGENTS/packet/checkout read 0.37.0.
- F-SG124-7 (minor): the vendor's rate table labels the s.jina.ai row "Reader API" in its Product column; the row's description
